 MultiBearer multilogin, ENABLE_SYNC and logout.
 
+## Page login state
+
+`GET /` and `GET /api/session` read the same `SID` cookie that Chromium's
+sign-in flow creates. If the browser is signed in, the status page shows the
+account and `/api/session` returns:
+
+```json
+{
+  "signedIn": true,
+  "primary": {"email": "test@example.com", "gaiaId": "…", "primary": true},
+  "accounts": [{"email": "test@example.com", "position": 0, "primary": true}],
+  "session": {"createdAt": 0, "expiresAt": 0, "deviceName": "", "ip": "…"}
+}
+```
+
+This is only the **login state of this service's origin**. It does not make
+`google.com` show the account (different cookie domain), and it is not Chrome
+Sync. Bookmark/history sync needs a separate `--sync-url` backend.
+
 ## Current limitations
 
 - **Sync (bookmarks, history, …) is not implemented.** Sign-in works and the
